  "body": "## What happens\n\nThe LinuxCNC post (`assets/posts/linuxcnc.cps`, PR #2310) writes `G73` for a `PECK` cycle and `G85` for a `REAM` cycle. The LinuxCNC G-code reference gives `G73` and `G85` no P word. When the cycle has a dwell (`PARAM P` > 0), the post writes the cycle block and the dwell is lost. The post shows no message.\n\n`assets/posts/tormach.cps` on `main` has the same pattern for `G73`. Its `REAM` cycle also posts `G85` and drops a dwell.\n\n## Expected\n\nThe post refuses a positive `G73` or `G85` dwell by name before it writes the cycle block. The refusal uses the text of the G83 refusal of #2348: `canned cycle G73 (...) dwell is not supported by this post - a <s> s dwell is refused, not dropped; set the dwell to 0`. A cycle with no dwell posts as before.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Review of PR #2310 (non-blocker 1): `linuxcnc.cps` `onCycle`, the `PECK` and `REAM` cycle maps and the P word line.\n- #2356 fixed the same defect on the Fanuc, Haas, Mazak and Doosan posts. #2354 fixed it on Sinumerik.\n- #2348 fixed the `G83` dwell on grblHAL and Tormach. PR #2310 copies that fix to LinuxCNC.\n\n## Done means\n\n- `linuxcnc.cps` and `tormach.cps` refuse a positive `G73` and `G85` dwell by name. Check `grblhal.cps` too.\n- A test in `crates/post/tests/` pins the refusal for each post, and pins that a zero dwell posts the cycle as before.\n",
